    <node id="publication:35273789">
      <data key="d1">publication</data>
      <data key="d2">PMID 35273789</data>
      <data key="d3">35273789</data>
      <data key="d4">Clozapine- and non-clozapine-associated neutropenia in patients with schizophrenia: a retrospective cohort study.</data>
      <data key="d5">2022</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:35273789:1:00083">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">supported evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">35273789</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
      <data key="d7">INTRODUCTION: The antipsychotic drug clozapine remains underutilized partly because of the risk of life-threatening adverse effects, such as neutropenia.</data>
      <data key="d8">supported</data>
      <data key="d9">[{"type": "risk_language", "text": "risk of", "start": 91, "end": 98}]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:35273789:3:00084">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">35273789</data>
      <data key="d6">3</data>
      <data key="d7">METHODS: In this retrospective cohort study, we used registry-based data from the Capital Region of Denmark to investigate incidence rates of neutropenia among patients with a diagnosis of schizophrenia or other psychotic disorders and treated with clozapine for the first time.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:35273789:4:00085">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">35273789</data>
      <data key="d6">4</data>
      <data key="d7">In a within-subject design, we compared rates of neutropenia in time periods where patients were exposed to clozapine &lt;i&gt;versus&lt;/i&gt; time periods, where they were not exposed to clozapine.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:35273789:5:00086">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">35273789</data>
      <data key="d6">5</data>
      <data key="d7">We also investigated whether the lengths of clozapine-associated neutropenia (CAN) were related to discontinuation of clozapine treatment.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:35273789:8:00087">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">35273789</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">There was no significant difference in incidence rates of neutropenia during clozapine exposure and non-clozapine exposure, with an incidence rate ratio of 0.7 (95% CI: 0.4-1.3).</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"kind": "negation", "text": "no ", "start": 10, "end": 13}]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:35273789:11:00088">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">speculative evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">35273789</data>
      <data key="d6">11</data>
      <data key="d7">CONCLUSION: In the present study, we could not confirm that clozapine treatment was associated with neutropenia.</data>
      <data key="d8">speculative</data>
      <data key="d9">[{"type": "associated", "text": "associated with", "start": 84, "end": 99}]</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"kind": "speculation", "text": "could", "start": 37, "end": 42}]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
