      <data key="d5">2026 Feb 06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:41651559:1:00277">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">supported evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">41651559</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
      <data key="d7">BACKGROUND: Clozapine is highly effective for treatment-resistant schizophrenia but has been associated with an increased risk of agranulocytosis.</data>
      <data key="d8">supported</data>
      <data key="d9">[{"type": "associated", "text": "associated with", "start": 93, "end": 108}, {"type": "risk_language", "text": "increased risk of", "start": 112, "end": 129}]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">3.949862763670301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:41651559:2:00278">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">41651559</data>
      <data key="d6">2</data>
      <data key="d7">As a result, until 2025, the Food and Drug Administration required patients receiving clozapine to undergo regular blood testing to monitor for neutropenia as part of a Risk Evaluation and Mitigation Strategy (REMS) programme.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:41651559:3:00279">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">supported evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">41651559</data>
      <data key="d6">3</data>
      <data key="d7">OBJECTIVE: This study sought to compare the risk of neutropenia-related hospitalisations between clozapine and olanzapine initiators.</data>
      <data key="d8">supported</data>
      <data key="d9">[{"type": "risk_language", "text": "risk of", "start": 44, "end": 51}]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:41651559:9:00280">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">41651559</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">At 6 months postinitiation, there were 12 neutropenia-related hospitalisations among the clozapine cohort (incidence rate: 2.21 per 1000 person-years; 95% CI 1.25 to 3.89) and &lt;11 among the olanzapine cohort (0.18; 95% CI 0.03 to 1.29), corresponding to an incidence rate ratio (IRR) of 12.18 (95% CI 1.58 to 93.71).</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:41651559:12:00281">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">supported evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">41651559</data>
      <data key="d6">12</data>
      <data key="d7">CONCLUSIONS: Clozapine initiators had an elevated risk of neutropenia-related hospitalisation, especially during the first 6 months of treatment, although the absolute risk was low.</data>
      <data key="d8">supported</data>
      <data key="d9">[{"type": "risk_language", "text": "elevated risk of", "start": 41, "end": 57}]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:41651559:13:00282">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">41651559</data>
      <data key="d6">13</data>
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL IMPLICATIONS: Despite removal of the REMS programme, it is important for prescribers to monitor patients for neutropenia after initiating clozapine.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="publication:41052486">
      <data key="d1">publication</data>
      <data key="d2">PMID 41052486</data>
      <data key="d3">41052486</data>
      <data key="d4">A retrospective study on clozapine-induced blood dyscrasias in the first 20 weeks of therapy.</data>
      <data key="d5">2025 Nov</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:41052486:1:00283">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">supported evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">41052486</data>
