      <data key="d7">OBJECTIVE: To review recent work on the haematological toxicity of clozapine and some other drugs used in psychiatry concerning especially (i) the mechanism of antipsychotic-induced neutropenia/agranulocytosis, (ii) criteria for clozapine prescribing in benign ethnic neutropenia, (iii) options in the event of worrying falls in white cell count (WCC), including measures to boost WCC with or without continued clozapine administration, (iv) criteria for clozapine rechallenge in the event that treatment was suspended because of a fall in WCC and (v) safety concerns regarding clozapine in children/adolescents.</data>
