    <node id="evidence:36620672:6:00364">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">36620672</data>
      <data key="d6">6</data>
      <data key="d7">In this case, clozapine was used for over 15 years, without neutropenia development.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"kind": "negation", "text": "without ", "start": 52, "end": 60}]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:36620672:7:00365">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">36620672</data>
      <data key="d6">7</data>
      <data key="d7">However, severe neutropenia (absolute neutrophil count = 523/μl) developed 3 days after the coadministration of Paxlovid 2 doses per day, valproic acid 1,000 mg per day and clozapine 100 mg per day.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:36620672:8:00366">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">36620672</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">The development of neutropenia may be attributed to the complicated interaction among Paxlovid, SARS-CoV-2 infection, valproic acid, fluvoxamine and clozapine.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"kind": "speculation", "text": "may", "start": 31, "end": 34}]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:36620672:11:00367">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">supported evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">36620672</data>
      <data key="d6">11</data>
      <data key="d7">Although the exact causes of neutropenia in this patient are not fully clear, the white blood cell count and absolute neutrophil count should be closely monitored during the administration of Paxlovid in clozapine-treated patients with SARS-CoV-2 infection.</data>
      <data key="d8">supported</data>
