      <data key="d7">BACKGROUND: Clozapine is the antipsychotic most associated with causing neutropenia, a reduction of absolute neutrophil count (ANC) to less than 1500 cells/μL, but neutropenia can also occur with other second-generation antipsychotics (SGAs).</data>
