    <node id="evidence:10340918:5:00810">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">10340918</data>
      <data key="d6">5</data>
      <data key="d7">RESULTS: In microsomal incubations, clozapine significantly increased the cell death in all groups: control subjects (8.8%+/-1.6%), control patients (7.4%+/-0.4%), and patients with agranulocytosis (9.1%+/-1.5%).</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">3.949862763670301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:10340918:7:00811">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">10340918</data>
      <data key="d6">7</data>
      <data key="d7">In similar incubations with HRP-H2O2, clozapine significantly increased toxicity (P &lt; .05) in cells from patients with agranulocytosis (22%+/-4.6%) compared with those from normal control subjects (7.7%+/-4.1%) or control patients (6.5%+/-4.4%).</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
