    <node id="publication:15076018">
      <data key="d1">publication</data>
      <data key="d2">PMID 15076018</data>
      <data key="d3">15076018</data>
      <data key="d4">Experience of maintaining clozapine medication in patients with 'red-alert zone' neutropenia: long-term follow-up results.</data>
      <data key="d5">2004 Mar</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:15076018:1:00857">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">15076018</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
      <data key="d7">According to the recommended guidelines by Novartis, neutropenia in the range of a white blood cell count less than 3000 per mm, or an absolute neutrophil count (ANC) less than 1500 per mm, is classified as being in the 'red-alert zone' during clozapine treatment.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:15076018:4:00858">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">15076018</data>
      <data key="d6">4</data>
      <data key="d7">Through retrospective chart reviews, five patients who had been maintained on clozapine treatment despite red-alert zone neutropenia were selected.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:15076018:5:00859">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">15076018</data>
      <data key="d6">5</data>
      <data key="d7">The haematological and clinical courses of these patients were followed for more than 600 days and were compared with those of two control patients who discontinued clozapine due to neutropenia.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:15076018:6:00860">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">15076018</data>
      <data key="d6">6</data>
      <data key="d7">In all five patients, no additional episodes of neutropenia occurred during the observation period despite continued clozapine treatment.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"kind": "negation", "text": "no ", "start": 22, "end": 25}]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">4.379310388184409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="evidence:15076018:10:00861">
      <data key="d1">evidence</data>
      <data key="d2">co_mention evidence</data>
      <data key="d3">15076018</data>
      <data key="d6">10</data>
      <data key="d7">However, while the guidelines for the prevention of agranulocytosis should be generally followed, it may be that judicious continuation of clozapine treatment is less risk-prone than previously considered in selected cases where only a few feasible alternatives to clozapine are available.</data>
      <data key="d8">co_mention</data>
      <data key="d9">[]</data>
      <data key="d10">[{"kind": "speculation", "text": "may", "start": 101, "end": 104}]</data>
      <data key="d11">case_study_lexicon_pair_scoped_rule_baseline</data>
      <data key="d12">3.949862763670301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="publication:12506270">
